+        <anchor xml:id=3D"c8e9d4"/>
+      </title>
+      <interlinear-gloss>
+        <jbo>coi la frank.</jbo>
+        <gloss>Hello, the-one-named=20
+        <quote>Frank</quote>.</gloss>
+      </interlinear-gloss>
+    </example>
+    <para>Syntactically, vocative phrases are a kind of free modifier, and=
 can appear in many places in Lojban text, generally at the beginning or en=
d of some complete construct; or, as in=20
+    <xref linkend=3D"example-random-id-qMG8"/> to=20
+    <xref linkend=3D"example-random-id-qmgM"/>, as sentences by themselves=
.</para>
+    <para> <indexterm type=3D"general-imported"><primary>vocative phrase w=
ith name</primary><secondary>placement of relative clause on</secondary></i=
ndexterm>  <indexterm type=3D"general-imported"><primary>relative clauses</=
primary><secondary>placement with vocative phrases</secondary></indexterm> =
 <indexterm type=3D"general-imported"><primary>vocative phrases</primary><s=
econdary>relative clauses on</secondary></indexterm>  <indexterm type=3D"ge=
neral-imported"><primary>relative clauses</primary><secondary>on vocative p=
hrases</secondary></indexterm> As can be seen, the form of vocative phrases=
 is similar to that of sumti, and as you might expect, vocative phrases all=
ow relative clauses in various places. In vocative phrases which are simple=
 names (after the vocative words), any relative clauses must come just afte=
r the names:</para>
+    <example role=3D"interlinear-gloss-example" xml:id=3D"example-random-i=
d-xECX">
