+    <para>The restrictive relative clause in=20
+   =20
+    <xref linkend=3D"example-random-id-xECX"/> suggests that there is some=
 other Frank (perhaps on the Green Team) from whom this Frank, the one the =
speaker is greeting, must be distinguished.</para>
+    <para> <indexterm type=3D"general-imported"><primary>vocative phrase w=
ith selbri</primary><secondary>placement of relative clause on</secondary><=
/indexterm> A vocative phrase containing a selbri can have relative clauses=
 either before or after the selbri; both forms have the same meaning. Here =
are some examples:</para>
+   =20
+    <example xml:id=3D"example-random-id-qmgV" role=3D"interlinear-gloss-e=
xample">
+      <title>
+        <anchor xml:id=3D"c8e9d6"/>
+      </title>
+      <interlinear-gloss>
+        <jbo>co'o poi mi zvati ke'a ku'o xirma</jbo>
