+      </title>
+      <interlinear-gloss>
+        <jbo>mi viska do fi'o kanla [fe'u] le zunle</jbo>
+        <gloss>I see you [modal] eye: the left-thing</gloss>
+        <natlang>I see you with the left eye.</natlang>
+      </interlinear-gloss>
+    </example>
+    <para> <indexterm type=3D"general-imported"><primary>fi'o with selbri<=
/primary><secondary>meaning of</secondary></indexterm>  <indexterm type=3D"=
general-imported"><primary>modal tag</primary><secondary>fi'o with selbri a=
s</secondary></indexterm>  <indexterm type=3D"general-imported"><primary>fi=
'o</primary><secondary>effect on following selbri</secondary></indexterm> T=
he three-place relation=20
+    <valsi>viska</valsi> has now acquired a fourth place specifying the ey=
e used for seeing. The combination of the cmavo=20
+    <valsi>fi'o</valsi> (of selma'o FIhO) followed by a selbri, in this ca=
se the gismu=20
+    <valsi>kanla</valsi>, forms a tag which is prefixed to the sumti filli=
ng the new place, namely=20
+    <jbophrase>le zunle</jbophrase>. The semantics of=20
+    <jbophrase>fi'o kanla le zunle</jbophrase> is that=20
+    <jbophrase>le zunle</jbophrase> fills the x1 place of=20
+    <valsi>kanla</valsi>, whose place structure is</para>
