secondary>before vowels</secondary></indexterm> The cmavo=20
-    <valsi>u'e</valsi> begins with a vowel, and like all words beginning w=
ith a vowel, requires a pause (represented by=20
-    <letteral>.</letteral>) before it. This pause cannot be omitted simply=
 because the cmavo is incorporated into a compound cmavo. On the other hand=
,</para>
