-   =20
-    <valsi>bo</valsi> of selma'o BO. Syntactically, you can prefix a sumti=
 qualifier to any sumti and produce another simple sumti. (You may need to =
add the elidable terminator=20
-   =20
-    <valsi>lu'u</valsi> to show where the qualified sumti ends.)</para>
-   =20
-    <para> <indexterm type=3D"general-imported"><primary>sumti qualifiers<=
/primary><secondary>as short forms for common special cases</secondary></in=
dexterm> Semantically, sumti qualifiers represent short forms of certain co=
mmon special cases. Suppose you want to say=20
-    <quote>I see 'The Red Pony'</quote>, where=20
-   =20
-    <quote>The Red Pony</quote> is the title of a book. How about:</para>
