-    <para>Here B's sentence repeats A's within an abstraction (explained i=
n <xref linkend=3D"chapter-abstractions"/>):=20
-    <jbophrase>le si'o mi go'i</jbophrase> means=20
-    <jbophrase>le si'o mi klama le zarci</jbophrase>. Why must B use the w=
ord=20
-    <valsi>mi</valsi> explicitly to replace the x1 of=20
-    <jbophrase>mi klama le zarci</jbophrase>, even though it looks like=20
-    <valsi>mi</valsi> is replacing=20
-    <valsi>mi</valsi>? Because B's=20
-    <valsi>mi</valsi> refers to B, whereas A's=20
-    <valsi>mi</valsi> refers to A. If B said:</para>
-    <example role=3D"interlinear-gloss-example" xml:id=3D"example-random-i=
d-2uS7">
